%% HANDWRITTEN. Checked against D9 + D30 + INTEGRATIONS.md S2
flowchart LR
    MIC["caller leg audio<br/>8kHz mu-law from the PSTN"]:::in
    MIC --> RS["resample to 16kHz mono"]:::step
    RS --> VAD["<b>VAD endpointing</b><br/>find where an utterance ENDS"]:::step
    VAD --> SEG["segment into utterances<br/>not fixed chunks"]:::step
    SEG --> Q["queue to a WORKER PROCESS<br/>never the event loop"]:::step
    Q --> M["<b>Thonburian Whisper</b><br/>biodatlab/whisper-th-medium-combined"]:::model
    M --> TURN["TranscriptTurn<br/>text + timings + asr_confidence + engine"]:::out
    TURN --> BUS["event bus -> brief builder + workstation"]:::out

    ALT["<b>alternatives benchmarked on the same audio (D30)</b><br/>- faster-whisper / CTranslate2 int8_float16<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;(probably REQUIRED to hit latency on a 3050)<br/>- Typhoon ASR<br/>- cloud STT as the fallback adapter"]:::note

    GPU["<b>the 3050 constraint.</b> 4-6GB. Whisper pads every<br/>chunk to 30s regardless of real length, which is why<br/>segmentation matters so much. Do NOT plan to run a<br/>local LLM and Whisper on the same card - the default<br/>split is STT local, LLM via API."]:::warn

    WHY["<b>why re-implement rather than copy the old project?</b><br/>The reference code is FILE-BASED: record, then transcribe.<br/>This system needs streaming - partial results while the<br/>customer is still talking. Different shape entirely,<br/>so it is reference for model behaviour, not code to copy. (D9)"]:::note

